+# Grounded inventory and recovery implementation plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** Implement natively in this session, one tested change at a time. Preserve the existing runtime and contribution workflow.
+
+**Goal:** Prevent custom-item misidentification and repeated infeasible Minecraft tasks using received inventory, actual capabilities and recent task outcomes.
+
+**Architecture:** Share readable item identity between native inventory queries and game snapshots. Reserve compact decision space for operational supplies. Keep a bounded, session-scoped outcome journal in the Minecraft plugin, and attach recovery facts to autonomous decisions. All game actions remain selected by Neko through existing tools.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node ESM/Mineflayer; Python asyncio/N.E.K.O. Minecraft plugin; existing node:test and unittest suites.
+
+**Spec:** The user's request to investigate and optimize the agent, plus `D:/neko-mc-trial/neko-progress-audit-20261009-170136.json`, `focus-readonly-check-20261009.json` and the 13:56–17:03 runtime logs. The agent has a blaze_rod with server wand lore but reports it missing, then repeatedly orders underground mining without a pickaxe, workbench or wood.
+
+## Global constraints
+
+- Keep `ag_NEKO`, local `http://127.0.0.1:18030/v1`, the desktop Neko and LAN viewer.
+- Change no server code, permissions or other agents.
+- Neko edits stay within `plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/`.
+- Do not inject diagnostic game actions, chat, commands or spells. Validate deployment through read-only observations of Neko's own actions.
+- Preserve running state; do not overwrite the supervisor's dirty arbitration file or persona/memory unrelated to the fixes.
+- Publish native fixes and Neko companion patches to the existing `jcs130/mc-agent-neko` fork branch.
+
+## Review focus
+
+- Modern NBT-wrapped text, legacy JSON names and lore must use the same identity path; labels do not grant instruction privileges.
+- Compact callback budgets must retain absent tools and carried wood/workstations, including slots after the first sixteen entries.
+- Durability beyond a library maximum is inconsistent evidence, not proof that a tool is usable or broken.
+- Reconnection, overwritten tasks and foreign/duplicate task completions must not poison the current recovery journal.
+- Existing control ownership, protection checks, player chat routing, stop requests and adaptive heartbeat behavior must remain intact.
+
+## Task 1: Read and expose custom item identity
+
+**Files:** Create `src/agent/library/item_identity.js`; modify `src/websocket/game_information.js`, `src/agent/commands/queries.js`; add `test/item_identity.test.mjs` and snapshot/query regressions.
+
+**Interface:** `readItemIdentity(item)` returns bounded base name, custom label and lore. Native `!inventory` keeps existing counts and adds readable, slot-addressed custom items. Snapshot items use the same helper.
+
+- [ ] Add modern and legacy fixtures, including `custom_name.data={type:'compound',value:{text:{type:'string',value:''},extra:{type:'list',value:{type:'compound',value:[{text:{type:'string',value:'灵纹法杖'}}]}}}}`.
+- [ ] Assert `collectGameState(agent).inventory.slots[0].customName === '灵纹法杖'` and actual native inventory output contains both `blaze_rod` and the server label/lore. Existing replay already fails with `'' !== '灵纹法杖'`.
+- [ ] Implement bounded readable identity, preserving base IDs for commands and handling unavailable getters independently.
+- [ ] Run `node --test test/item_identity.test.mjs test/game_information.test.mjs test/mission_observations.test.mjs` and commit the verified slice.
+
+## Task 2: Preserve operational supplies in compact decisions
+
+**Files:** `observations.py`, `test_observations.py`, new `test_grounded_recovery.py` inside this plugin.
+
+**Interface:** Compact context adds a protected `resources` summary from all received inventory counts/slots: pickaxes and condition, actual logs/planks/sticks, workstations, iron materials and named-item/base-ID pairs. Missing inventory remains unknown; ordinary verbose inventory remains queryable.
+
+- [ ] Replay the captured 17:01 inventory with a normalized wand label. Assert the label and explicit empty pickaxe list survive `context(max_tokens=400)`; the current replay loses inventory entirely.
+- [ ] Add cases for a tool in a late slot, adequate carried crafting supplies, inconsistent durability and stale/missing inventory.
+- [ ] Implement bounded resource extraction and budget reduction that trims optional details before operational facts.
+- [ ] Verify both standalone summary and complete autonomous callback token counts, preserving protection/collision regressions.
+- [ ] Run the focused unittest modules and commit the verified slice.
+
+## Task 3: Carry failure history into recovery decisions
+
+**Files:** `service.py`, `prompts.py`, `test_grounded_recovery.py`, existing completion/query-loop tests.
+
+**Interface:** A bounded session-scoped `recentTaskOutcomes` list and `failureStreak` supplement the existing `lastTaskOutcome`; only matched terminal tasks enter it. Idle decisions retain concise failure evidence and current resource prerequisites.
+
+- [ ] Feed two real matched failed completions through `_on_task_finished`; assert the next autonomous decision retains both blockers and a consecutive failure count.
+- [ ] Verify duplicate/foreign/retroactive completions cannot overwrite current history; new world/session clears the journal.
+- [ ] Add a concise recovery policy: verify prerequisites before dispatch, resolve one missing prerequisite, use actually documented recovery/communication paths after repeated failures, and avoid long wait chains in short tasks.
+- [ ] Re-run completion, observation, heartbeat, chat and query-loop tests, including the full callback budget.
+- [ ] Commit the verified slice.
+
+## Task 4: Check execution capabilities and deploy verified changes
+
+**Files:** Native command documentation/profile evidence, contribution `integrations/project-neko` patch bundle and deployment notes.
+
+- [ ] Compare the actual `getCommandDocs` output and runtime blocked-action list with false "no upward digging command" failures. Existing source exposes `!goToSurface` and `!pillarUp`; do not add duplicate skills.
+- [ ] If needed, add a short availability-filtered reminder at the existing command-doc boundary; prove it never advertises blocked or missing commands.
+- [ ] Run both complete project suites and inspect diffs for secrets, unrelated changes and temporary diagnostics.
+- [ ] Cherry-pick native commits into the contribution and live checkouts; export Neko plugin changes as companion patches and verify the patched plugin tree exactly matches the source tree.
+- [ ] Use the existing controlled lifecycle scripts to reload only required services, preserving the local LLM and user configuration.
+- [ ] Observe Neko's own autonomous decisions and real inventory/position changes. Report separately code correctness, live progress and remaining limitations; push verified commits to the fork.
+
+## Diagnosis record
+
+- Confirmed: current snapshot item naming fails on NBT-wrapped modern custom text; native `!inventory` returns only counts and armor IDs.
+- Confirmed: replaying the real crowded inventory at 400 tokens produces `inventory={details:'minecraft_observe'}`; at 700 tokens it keeps only the first sixteen counts and drops named-item identity.
+- To verify: failure history/decision grounding and actual command availability at the native prompt boundary.
